## Why This Is Asked
Tests multilingual orchestration, privacy, and end-to-end data flow in Azure OpenAI pipelines.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Translator Text API
- Azure Cognitive Search over Blob KB
- Text Analytics for PII redaction
- Cosmos DB per-tenant language settings
- Durable Functions orchestration
- API Management as a gateway

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo code for flow
async function handleQuery(userQuery, tenantId) {
  const lang = await getTenantLang(tenantId);
  const enQuery = await translateToEnglish(userQuery, lang);
  const answer = await groundKB(enQuery);
  const redacted = redactPII(answer, enQuery);
  return await translateFromEnglish(redacted, lang);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test translation fidelity and PII redaction in CI?
- How would you monitor latency across translation, search, and OpenAI calls?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical security-first design for Azure OpenAI with code-gen, focusing on secret redaction, key vault integration, tenant isolation, and auditable logging.

## Key Concepts
- Secret management with Azure Key Vault and Managed Identity
- Request/response redaction and policy enforcement
- Data isolation per tenant and private networking
- End-to-end auditing in Purview
- Testing: redaction fuzzing and integration tests

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: redact secrets before sending to OpenAI
function redact(input, keys){
  let out = input;
  keys.forEach(k => { out = out.replace(new RegExp(k, 'g'), 'REDACTED'); });
  return out;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test drift in redaction rules across tenants?
- What data plane logs would you guard and what retention policy would you apply?

## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses practical Azure OpenAI engineering skills for data generation with governance, privacy, and observability.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant data policy gating
- PII redaction using Text Analytics
- Grounding with Cognitive Search and versioned KB
- Auditable logging to Data Lake

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example pseudo-code: gate -> redact -> search -> openai
function handleInput(input, tenant) {
  if (!policyAllows(tenant, input)) throw new Error('Not allowed');
  const redacted = redactPII(input);
  const kb = searchKB(redacted, tenant);
  return callOpenAI(redacted, kb);
}
```

